{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1033448-how-to-do-certain-effects","id":1033448,"title":"how to do certain effects?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-17T10:32:22-08:00","id":1033448,"title":"how to do certain effects?","content":"a player of mine wanted to know<br /> How to break Match 1 using magick, both vulgar and coincidental.<br /> <br /> second: how to make the mirror reality/effect of doctor strange, like a pocket dimension to fight? (told him it would be vulgar as fuck)<br /> <br /> third: how to punch at the speed of sound or breaking match 1 using magick (he is a akashic)<br /> <br /> seriously, i think watching anime is giving him horrible ideas<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:54:40-08:00","id":1033466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1033448-how-to-do-certain-effects#post1033448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a player of mine wanted to know<br /> How to break Match 1 using magick, both vulgar and coincidental.<br /> <br /> second: how to make the mirror reality/effect of doctor strange, like a pocket dimension to fight? (told him it would be vulgar as fuck)<br /> <br /> third: how to punch at the speed of sound or breaking match 1 using magick (he is a akashic)<br /> <br /> seriously, i think watching anime is giving him horrible ideas<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to assume you mean &quot;Mach 1&quot;<br /> <br /> 1: Two ways, the first is a Forces (Either Forces 2 and a hell of a lot of successes on something small, or Forces 4 on something big) effect to increase the speed of whatever you're doing (running, flying, driving) to a great level. This will only be coincidental when used on things that you'd expect to break Mach 1 like say a Jet or a specially designed Rocket Car. For everything else, this is Vulgar, and may require Entropy 3 or Matter magic in order to avoid the entire thing falling apart. In order to run that fast, you'd probably need Life magic of Entropy 4 to avoid your entire body falling apart.<br /> <br /> The second way is to use Time magic (Time 3) to speed yourself or whatever you're in to those speeds. This would would be vulgar without question, but you wouldn't need Entropy, Matter, or Life in order to keep things from falling apart.<br /> <br /> 2. Two ways, the first is with Correspondence (Corr 4 with a ton of successes for a smallish space, Corr 5 for a much larger one, and even higher for anything resembling Doctor Strange). You are literally folding the corners of space around to make a world within a world completely separate from mundane space. Go you.<br /> There's no two ways about it, this is vulgar.<br /> <br /> The Second way is using Spirit (Spirit 3 to cross over into the spirit world, spirit 5 with Correspondence to create a new section of Umbra). If you're crossing over into the Penumbra, you'll have something vaguely resembling what happened in Doctor Strange, in that it will mirror the world around you, but will not actually be there. Sleepers will be almost entirely invisible, while Mages will leave dark shadows. A lot of fights can take place here with minimal damage to the mundane world (though destroying a building's umbral counterpart will probably have an affect on the mundane one). However, spirits lurk in the penumbra, who may be a bit annoyed if you start fighting at their doorstep.<br /> Making a completely new spirit realm is an epic undertaking and probably not worth the effort for creating a private fighting hall.<br /> Either way, Vulgar.<br /> <br /> Another alternative is to have the world take from in their head with Mind 3. In this case you're creating a world so much as putting the two of you in a shared imagined space. This would be coincidental but can be shrugged off with a Willpower roll.<br /> <br /> 3. Forces all the way. This will be Vulgar unless you happen to be in a culture that accepts that Warrior Monks are just capable of that kind of stuff. Forces 2 for the punch, again you may need Life or Entropy 4 to keep your hand from falling apart, or whatever other precautions you can think off.<br /> You can use Time for this as per the previous effect, but doing so would only make the punch faster, it wouldn't change the impact. Though Time magic would be necessary if you want to do crazy Dragon Ball Z things like drumming off 20 punches per second.<br /> Again, unless the locals believe that Warrior Monks are capable of this kind of stuff, it's vulgar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-17-2017, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T12:45:17-08:00","id":1033566,"title":"","content":"that reminds me, is there a way to &quot;teleport&quot; with out making it vulgar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T13:14:16-08:00","id":1033585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1033448-how-to-do-certain-effects?p=1033566#post1033566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that reminds me, is there a way to &quot;teleport&quot; with out making it vulgar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Be in the umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T14:00:04-08:00","id":1033623,"title":"","content":"In your Dreams (somewhat similar to the Umbra but easier to enter)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T02:29:53-08:00","id":1033929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1033448-how-to-do-certain-effects?p=1033566#post1033566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that reminds me, is there a way to &quot;teleport&quot; with out making it vulgar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Drop a smoke grenade or flashbang. So long as there's a way your character could logically have left the area (a door, hallway, street, etc), most Average Observers would more readily chalk it up to the character sneaking away, than jumping to the conclusion that you teleported. Darkness is also good for this, so running into a dark room or taking out all the lights is acceptable.<br /> <br /> Some people on this forum might raise their hackles at this sort of loose interpretation of Hypothetical Average Observer, but I find that you need to be forgiving in this regard. No one wants to play a game of Mage where nothing is considered Coincidental. Do what seems most cinematic or story appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T02:46:23-08:00","id":1033933,"title":"","content":"Oh boy. I'm not going to start going down that rabbit hole again.<br /> Here's the thread where we discuss this point to death.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence\"> Teleportation and Coincidence - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I tend to assume that teleportation of yourself or another person can't be done Coincidentally outside the Umbra and Sanctums and the like. Moving an object from one concealed location to another would be Coincidental under HAP, but the idea that someone could step into a walk-in closet in Toronto and Coincidentally come out of a walk-in closet in Rio de Jinero never seemed right to me. I think I've figured out why. When I think of a Hypothetical Average Observer observing a teleporting mage, I don't think of them just being in the departure point and arrival point--I think of the Observer as going </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One thing I will say if teleporting away isn't the only thing you should consider when determining vulgarity. You should also consider where you teleport to an how that would look if someone was right next to your destination as you pop in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:47:18-08:00","id":1034142,"title":"","content":"I am with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a> on this, as long as it is a short range teleportation or alternatively with a sanctum as destination.<br /> <br /> Funny thing with colocation: You are on 3 distinct places at once, you decide to end colocation number 1. Vulgarity is checked for when you cast a spell, not when you dismiss one. But it looks quite vulgar... yet isn't RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:44:09-08:00","id":1034219,"title":"","content":"Alternative on the Mirror effect: if you assuming such a Realm just existing in the Umbra, you can do with Spirit 3 alone. Strange seems to actually follow this path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}